554
00:21:00,560 --> 00:21:02,560
I mean, I have lots of sheath knives

555
00:21:02,560 --> 00:21:04,560
and I use them from time to time,

556
00:21:04,560 --> 00:21:06,560
but my pocket knife is more useful.

557
00:21:06,560 --> 00:21:08,560
And I'll add that

558
00:21:08,560 --> 00:21:10,560
common sense leads us to conclude

559
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:12,560
that sheath knives that were designed

560
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:13,560
principally for weapons

561
00:21:13,560 --> 00:21:14,560
or as hunting knives

562
00:21:14,560 --> 00:21:16,560
they're not going to be a whole lot

563
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:17,560
of use to scouts.

564
00:21:17,560 --> 00:21:19,560
I don't have a problem with them,

565
00:21:19,560 --> 00:21:21,560
I just don't think they're all that useful.

566
00:21:21,560 --> 00:21:23,560
So, to kind of wrap it all together,

567
00:21:23,560 --> 00:21:25,560
we want our scouts to be able to use knives.

568
00:21:25,560 --> 00:21:27,560
They're an invaluable back country tool.

569
00:21:27,560 --> 00:21:29,560
We want them to do it safely,

570
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:30,560
but we don't want to turn ourselves

571
00:21:30,560 --> 00:21:32,560
into the knife police. right,

572
00:21:32,560 --> 00:21:34,560
Theoretically, can a scout carry a sheath knife?

573
00:21:34,560 --> 00:21:36,560
but we want to avoid sheath knives.

574
00:21:36,560 --> 00:21:38,560
I think part of it's a safety matter,

575
00:21:38,560 --> 00:21:40,560
but part of it's also

576
00:21:40,560 --> 00:21:42,560
that they're really just not that useful.

577
00:21:42,560 --> 00:21:44,560
Jay, I hope that helps you sort this out.

578
00:21:44,560 --> 00:21:46,560
I also heard from Sean Keeney,

579
00:21:46,560 --> 00:21:48,560
and Sean is an assistant cub master

580
00:21:48,560 --> 00:21:51,560
with PAC 70 in Foxborough, Massachusetts.

581
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:53,560
He wrote in to say this:

582
00:21:53,560 --> 00:21:55,560
We are going on a PAC overnight in November.

583
00:21:55,560 --> 00:21:57,560
An older brother of one of our cubs

584
00:21:57,560 --> 00:21:59,560
who just joined Boy Scouts

585
00:21:59,560 --> 00:22:00,560
will be coming along.

586
00:22:00,560 --> 00:22:02,560
I'd like him to have an active part of the trip

587
00:22:02,560 --> 00:22:04,560
and be kind of like our den chief

588
00:22:04,560 --> 00:22:05,560
for the weekend.

589
00:22:05,560 --> 00:22:06,560
My question is this:

590
00:22:06,560 --> 00:22:08,560
will his participation in the overnight

591
00:22:08,560 --> 00:22:10,560
and activities on our camp out

592
00:22:10,560 --> 00:22:12,560
count towards his advancement

593
00:22:12,560 --> 00:22:13,560
towards Tenderfoot?

594
00:22:13,560 --> 00:22:15,560
Thanks for the podcast.

595
00:22:15,560 --> 00:22:17,560
I stumbled across it a few months ago

596
00:22:17,560 --> 00:22:18,560
and I look forward to it each week.

597
00:22:18,560 --> 00:22:20,560
Sean, thanks so much for listening.

598
00:22:20,560 --> 00:22:22,560
I'm glad you're enjoying the podcast.

599
00:22:22,560 --> 00:22:24,560
Thank you for being such a generous

600
00:22:24,560 --> 00:22:25,560
assistant cub master

601
00:22:25,560 --> 00:22:27,560
and working to include this scout.

602
00:22:27,560 --> 00:22:29,560
make his experience a good one

603
00:22:29,560 --> 00:22:31,560
when he goes camping with the PAC.

604
00:22:31,560 --> 00:22:33,560
The first thing that we can do

605
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:34,560
to answer your question

606
00:22:34,560 --> 00:22:36,560
is carefully read Tenderfoot

607
00:22:36,560 --> 00:22:37,560
requirement number two,

608
00:22:37,560 --> 00:22:38,560
And it says this:

609
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:40,560
Spend at least one night

610
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:42,560
on a patrol or troop camp out.

611
00:22:42,560 --> 00:22:44,560
Sleep in a tent. you have helped pitch.

612
00:22:44,560 --> 00:22:46,560
If we read that requirement carefully,

613
00:22:46,560 --> 00:22:48,560
we see the words troop

614
00:22:48,560 --> 00:22:50,560
and patrol. that's specified.

615
00:22:50,560 --> 00:22:52,560
It's not a PAC or a den camp out.

616
00:22:52,560 --> 00:22:54,560
So nights camping with the PAC

617
00:22:54,560 --> 00:22:56,560
or den do not count

618
00:22:56,560 --> 00:22:58,560
towards this requirement

619
00:22:58,560 --> 00:23:00,560
unless the whole patrol is there

620
00:23:00,560 --> 00:23:02,560
or unless the whole troop is there.

621
00:23:02,560 --> 00:23:04,560
If we look at Tenderfoot requirement number three,

622
00:23:04,560 --> 00:23:06,560
it says this: on the camp out,

623
00:23:06,560 --> 00:23:08,560
assist in preparing and cooking

624
00:23:08,560 --> 00:23:10,560
one of your patrol's meals.

625
00:23:10,560 --> 00:23:12,560
Tell why it is important for each patrol member

626
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:14,560
to share and meal preparation

627
00:23:14,560 --> 00:23:15,560
and clean up

628
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:17,560
and explain the importance of eating together.

629
00:23:17,560 --> 00:23:20,560
Your patrol in that requirement

630
00:23:20,560 --> 00:23:22,560
is not a den or a PAC

631
00:23:22,560 --> 00:23:24,560
or a troop for that matter.

632
00:23:24,560 --> 00:23:26,560
It's your patrol.

633
00:23:26,560 --> 00:23:27,560
What you see in these requirements

634
00:23:27,560 --> 00:23:29,560
is intended to get a scout

635
00:23:29,560 --> 00:23:31,560
into the life of his patrol.

636
00:23:31,560 --> 00:23:33,560
That's where all of scouting happens.

637
00:23:33,560 --> 00:23:35,560
It's not simply going camping

638
00:23:35,560 --> 00:23:37,560
or cooking a meal without any context.

639
00:23:37,560 --> 00:23:40,560
it's doing these things with your patrol.

640
00:23:40,560 --> 00:23:42,560
As for the other Tenderfoot requirements,

641
00:23:42,560 --> 00:23:44,560
an older scout could certainly

642
00:23:44,560 --> 00:23:45,560
learn and practice them

643
00:23:45,560 --> 00:23:46,560
on a Cub Scout camping trip

644
00:23:46,560 --> 00:23:48,560
If he has the time.

645
00:23:48,560 --> 00:23:50,560
but who's supposed to be signing them off?

646
00:23:50,560 --> 00:23:53,560
This is really the Scoutmasters prerogative.

647
00:23:53,560 --> 00:23:56,560
If they give you permission to sign them off,

648
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:57,560
well, that's fine.

649
00:23:57,560 --> 00:23:59,560
but most Scoutmasters will want

650
00:23:59,560 --> 00:24:01,560
patrol leaders signing requirements

651
00:24:01,560 --> 00:24:02,560
rather than adults.

652
00:24:02,560 --> 00:24:03,560
Once again,

653
00:24:03,560 --> 00:24:05,560
I think you're being very generous

654
00:24:05,560 --> 00:24:06,560
and very helpful

655
00:24:06,560 --> 00:24:08,560
and you're very right in theory

656
00:24:08,560 --> 00:24:10,560
to offer as much opportunity

657
00:24:10,560 --> 00:24:11,560
as you can for this scout.

658
00:24:11,560 --> 00:24:13,560
but scouting is something more

659
00:24:13,560 --> 00:24:15,560
than just checking things off a list

660
00:24:15,560 --> 00:24:17,560
to look at the requirements carefully.

661
00:24:17,560 --> 00:24:19,560
It's a lot about who we do things with

662
00:24:19,560 --> 00:24:21,560
and how they are done.

663
00:24:21,560 --> 00:24:23,560
that contextualizes the experience

664
00:24:23,560 --> 00:24:24,560
we want Scouts to have

665
00:24:24,560 --> 00:24:26,560
in fulfilling those requirements.

666
00:24:26,560 --> 00:24:28,560
David wrote in with this question.

667
00:24:28,560 --> 00:24:30,560
he said in my first year as Scoutmaster

668
00:24:30,560 --> 00:24:32,560
I've been able to keep adults

669
00:24:32,560 --> 00:24:33,560
out of the planning process

670
00:24:33,560 --> 00:24:35,560
and let the Scouts make decisions.

671
00:24:35,560 --> 00:24:36,560
At a recent meeting

672
00:24:36,560 --> 00:24:38,560
it was pointed out by a parent

673
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:39,560
that a Veterans Day parade

674
00:24:39,560 --> 00:24:40,560
we normally participate in

675
00:24:40,560 --> 00:24:42,560
wasn't on their schedule.

676
00:24:42,560 --> 00:24:44,560
Can I tell Scouts that they're in charge

677
00:24:44,560 --> 00:24:45,560
without adult interference

678
00:24:45,560 --> 00:24:47,560
and then turn around and tell them

679
00:24:47,560 --> 00:24:48,560
they have to schedule this parade

680
00:24:48,560 --> 00:24:50,560
because it's a traditional service

681
00:24:50,560 --> 00:24:52,560
that the troop does in the community?

682
00:24:52,560 --> 00:24:54,560
I think I would prefer that they

683
00:24:54,560 --> 00:24:56,560
originate their own service ideas.

684
00:24:56,560 --> 00:24:57,560
in all my efforts to give the Scouts

685
00:24:57,560 --> 00:24:59,560
free reign and how they do things,

686
00:24:59,560 --> 00:25:01,560
I am also running against

687
00:25:01,560 --> 00:25:03,560
a kind of counterproductive message

688
00:25:03,560 --> 00:25:05,560
on a part of some parents

689
00:25:05,560 --> 00:25:07,560
that they have to become Eagle Scouts.

690
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:09,560
I'd appreciate any advice

691
00:25:09,560 --> 00:25:11,560
you could give me on either of those matters.

692
00:25:11,560 --> 00:25:13,560
Hey, David, you know, this kind of conundrum

693
00:25:13,560 --> 00:25:15,560
comes up from time to time in any troop.

694
00:25:15,560 --> 00:25:17,560
I don't think you have to direct here.

695
00:25:17,560 --> 00:25:19,560
I think all you have to do

696
00:25:19,560 --> 00:25:21,560
is sit down with the patrol leader's council

697
00:25:21,560 --> 00:25:22,560
and explain the situation,

698
00:25:22,560 --> 00:25:24,560
just like you did to me in this email.

699
00:25:24,560 --> 00:25:25,560
You can sit down and say:

700
00:25:25,560 --> 00:25:27,560
listen, I'm really invested

701
00:25:27,560 --> 00:25:28,560
in your decision making,

702
00:25:28,560 --> 00:25:30,560
in the way that you put your calendar together,

703
00:25:30,560 --> 00:25:31,560
but it was brought to my attention

704
00:25:31,560 --> 00:25:32,560
that we didn't include

705
00:25:32,560 --> 00:25:34,560
the Veterans Day parade

706
00:25:34,560 --> 00:25:35,560
in your plans

707
00:25:35,560 --> 00:25:36,560
and I was wondering

708
00:25:36,560 --> 00:25:37,560
what you thought about that.

709
00:25:37,560 --> 00:25:38,560
Now, I'd imagine

710
00:25:38,560 --> 00:25:40,560
they probably like to do the parade anyway.

711
00:25:40,560 --> 00:25:41,560
maybe it was just an oversight

712
00:25:41,560 --> 00:25:42,560
on their part.

713
00:25:42,560 --> 00:25:44,560
maybe they really don't want to go

714
00:25:44,560 --> 00:25:45,560
and do the parade.

715
00:25:45,560 --> 00:25:46,560
You can take this opportunity

716
00:25:46,560 --> 00:25:47,560
to have a conversation

717
00:25:47,560 --> 00:25:49,560
about all the issues

718
00:25:49,560 --> 00:25:50,560
that this involves,

719
00:25:50,560 --> 00:25:51,560
and it will probably be

720
00:25:51,560 --> 00:25:53,560
a great conversation too.

721
00:25:53,560 --> 00:25:55,560
As far as parents

722
00:25:55,560 --> 00:25:57,560
who have in their mind

723
00:25:57,560 --> 00:25:58,560
that their boy

724
00:25:58,560 --> 00:26:00,560
must become an Eagle Scout,

725
00:26:00,560 --> 00:26:02,560
well, parents often

726
00:26:02,560 --> 00:26:04,560
don't get what we're trying to do.

727
00:26:04,560 --> 00:26:05,560
Remember that most of us

728
00:26:05,560 --> 00:26:06,560
didn't get it at first either,

729
00:26:06,560 --> 00:26:07,560
and given enough time,

730
00:26:07,560 --> 00:26:09,560
most of them will get on board,

731
00:26:09,560 --> 00:26:10,560
but some continue to pull

732
00:26:10,560 --> 00:26:12,560
in the other direction.

733
00:26:12,560 --> 00:26:14,560
If a Scout is on the fast track

734
00:26:14,560 --> 00:26:15,560
to Eagle because his parents

735
00:26:15,560 --> 00:26:16,560
are driving him.

736
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:17,560
I lend him all the support

737
00:26:17,560 --> 00:26:18,560
and encouragement I can.

738
00:26:18,560 --> 00:26:20,560
He has no control over

739
00:26:20,560 --> 00:26:21,560
what his parents do,

740
00:26:21,560 --> 00:26:22,560
and really neither do I.

741
00:26:22,560 --> 00:26:23,560
We can try talking

742
00:26:23,560 --> 00:26:24,560
and counseling

743
00:26:24,560 --> 00:26:25,560
and doing what we can,

744
00:26:25,560 --> 00:26:26,560
but remember

745
00:26:26,560 --> 00:26:28,560
we're not the boy's parent.

746
00:26:28,560 --> 00:26:30,560
we don't set the goals for him.

747
00:26:30,560 --> 00:26:31,560
we can advise

748
00:26:31,560 --> 00:26:32,560
and coach

749
00:26:32,560 --> 00:26:33,560
and mentor

750
00:26:33,560 --> 00:26:34,560
and see if we can help

751
00:26:34,560 --> 00:26:35,560
set the situation straight,

752
00:26:35,560 --> 00:26:36,560
but in no way

753
00:26:36,560 --> 00:26:37,560
do we want to penalize a Scout

754
00:26:37,560 --> 00:26:38,560
because his parents

755
00:26:38,560 --> 00:26:39,560
happen to be a little pushy

756
00:26:39,560 --> 00:26:40,560
or something like that.

757
00:26:40,560 --> 00:26:42,560
David, I hope that helps.

758
00:26:42,560 --> 00:26:43,560
I would love to have you again

759
00:26:43,560 --> 00:26:44,560
in touch with me

760
00:26:44,560 --> 00:26:45,560
and ask your questions

761
00:26:45,560 --> 00:26:46,560
about scouting,

762
00:26:46,560 --> 00:26:47,560
and I'll tell you how to do that

763
00:26:47,560 --> 00:26:48,560
in just a minute.

